Choose the API for your language. The Zig walkthrough below builds one
complete CapTP call. The C ABI and the language bindings offer the same
operations, each with its own conventions for ownership and concurrency.

> []($block.attrs('link-grid'))
> - [Zig]($link.ref('in-zig'))
> - [C or another FFI host]($link.ref('from-c-or-any-ffi-host'))
> - [Rust]($link.page('bindings/rust'))
> - [TypeScript]($link.page('bindings/ts'))
> - [Python]($link.page('bindings/python'))
> - [Racket]($link.page('bindings/racket'))
> - [In the browser]($link.page('bindings/browser'))

Pin a commit when you add glowcap to a project. The public API can still
change.

# [In Zig]($section.id('in-zig'))

glowcap is a [Zig](https://ziglang.org/) package. Add a pinned checkout to
your build:

```sh
zig fetch --save git+https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap#COMMIT_SHA
```

Replace `COMMIT_SHA` with the revision you want to pin.

```zig
const glowcap = b.dependency("glowcap", .{ .target = target, .optimize = optimize });
exe.root_module.addImport("glowcap", glowcap.module("glowcap"));
```

The `glowcap` module is pure Zig. The iroh, relay, and webrtc tabs below
import a transport module that links outside code:

```zig
// iroh: links a Rust library, so the build needs cargo on PATH.
exe.root_module.addImport("iroh", glowcap.module("glowcap_iroh"));
// noise-relay and keyed-relay: builds Mbed TLS from source.
exe.root_module.addImport("relay_tls", glowcap.module("glowcap_relay_tls"));
// webrtc: links a Rust library, so the build needs cargo on PATH.
exe.root_module.addImport("webrtc", glowcap.module("glowcap_webrtc"));
```

# Dial

Each tab sets up one transport, and the code after the tabs is the same for
all of them. Start with **noise-tcp**, TCP sealed with the
[Noise]($link.page('transports/noise')) protocol, between two peers that can
already reach each other. For a deployment, pick a row from
[Choosing a transport]($link.page('transports/choosing')) and use its tab.
Plain `tcp` is cleartext and for local tests only.

One iroh endpoint carries many connections, so the iroh tab registers it once and
every connection shares it. Everything after that works as it does on the other
transports.

